{"name":"King Neptune","hex":"#7794c0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"king","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A male monarch; a man who heads a monarchy; in an absolute monarchy, the supreme ruler of his nation.","The monarch with the most power and authority in a monarchy, regardless of sex."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To crown king, to make (a person) king.","To rule over as king."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/king"},{"term":"neptune","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A brass or copper pan used to evaporate salt water to obtain salt."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/neptune"}],"entries":[{"title":"Neptune (mythology)","blocks":[{"text":"Neptune is the god of freshwater and the sea in the Roman religion. He is the counterpart of the Greek god Poseidon. In the Greek-inspired tradition, he is a brother of Jupiter and Pluto, with whom he presides over the realms of heaven, the earthly world, and the seas. Salacia is his wife."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Sousse_neptune.jpg/330px-Sousse_neptune.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neptune_(mythology)","wikidata":"Q3954"},{"title":"King Neptune (pig)","blocks":[{"text":"King Neptune was a pig used by a United States Navy recruiter to raise $19 million in war bonds for the construction of the Iowa-class battleship Illinois between 1942 and 1946."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Pig_King_of_Mount_Pleasant.jpg/330px-Pig_King_of_Mount_Pleasant.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/King_Neptune_(pig)","wikidata":"Q6411908"},{"title":"King Neptune (film)","blocks":[{"text":"King Neptune is a 1932 animated short film produced by Walt Disney, and the second in the Silly Symphonies series to be produced in Technicolor. While Flowers and Trees was originally intended as a black and white cartoon, King Neptune was meant to be in color from the start, and was able to take full advantage of this."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/57/King_Neptune_%28Disney_film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/King_Neptune_(film)","wikidata":"Q3197023"},{"title":"King","blocks":[{"text":"King is a royal title given to a male monarch. A king is an absolute monarch if he holds unrestricted governmental power or exercises full sovereignty over a nation. In a modern context, the title may refer to the ruler of one of a number of modern monarchies. The title of king is used alongside other titles for monarchs: in the West, emperor, grand prince, prince, archduke, duke or grand duke, and in the Islamic world, malik, sultan, emir or hakim, among others."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Aachen_Domschatz_Bueste1.jpg/330px-Aachen_Domschatz_Bueste1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/King","wikidata":"Q12097"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Affreschi_romani_-_nettuno_anfitrine_-_pompei.JPG/500px-Affreschi_romani_-_nettuno_anfitrine_-_pompei.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Affreschi_romani_-_nettuno_anfitrine_-_pompei.JPG/1280px-Affreschi_romani_-_nettuno_anfitrine_-_pompei.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Affreschi_romani_-_nettuno_anfitrine_-_pompei.JPG/500px-Affreschi_romani_-_nettuno_anfitrine_-_pompei.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ichthyocentaur, Salacia and Neptune, antique fresco fro